  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Friday)\nIssued at 132 PM MDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nShowers and storms may linger across the east-southeast on Monday\ndue to residual moisture and a passing disturbance. However PWATs\nwill be gradually declining, reducing the overall flash flooding\nthreat. Drier air, increasing subsidence from weak ridging, and \nwest-southwesterly flow are expected to promoting warmer and \ndrier trends by midweek. The next system looks to approach the \nwestern CONUS by late week into next weekend, and the \naforementioned southwesterly flow will likely be able to tap into \nmore anomalous moisture to promote increasing rain chances. Long \nterm models suggest modest shear, but instability doesn't look as\nfavorable as the last couple of days. There is still a good bit of\ntime until we reach this point in the forecast, so expect greater\ndetails and forecast refinement in the coming days.",
